{
  "title": "OOP in modern JavaScript",
  "idea": "Object-oriented programming groups data with the methods that act on it, using encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance and polymorphism, plus composition for flexibility.",
  "points": [
    "Encapsulation: a `#private` field cannot be read from outside the class.",
    "Inheritance: `extends` reuses a parent; subclass constructors call `super()` before using `this`.",
    "Polymorphism: one call, `area()`, runs the method of the object's own class.",
    "Composition: a class holds other objects and delegates work to them."
  ],
